\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 's period piece, set in a ravaged, fallen Germany after the end of  World War II, is one that goes unresolved. All that's left are defensive denials, evasions of Nazi collaboration and the faint hope that something higher has survived. I could watch this kind of guilt-ridden post-apocalyptic movie for hours; instead, this lasts a scant 82 minutes. The conclusion, a wordless moment between father and daughter set to the strains of Bach played on a broken pipe organ, was the most devastating passage of the entire festival. "Fatherland" shows off Pawlikowski's exquisite way with black-and-white evocations of European tragedy, but he's never summed them up as poetically. - }
